<div class="doc-section">
    <h2>Events</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>Arg Type</th><th>Notes</th><th>Sample Pages</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td>OnSelectionChanged</td>
                <td>EventCallback&lt;NxGridSelectionArgs&lt;T&gt;&gt;</td>
                <td>Fires on every selection change — mouse, keyboard, or programmatic.</td>
                <td><a href="selection">Selection</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>SelectedItems</td>
                <td>List&lt;T&gt;?</td>
                <td>Two-way bindable list of all currently selected row objects (all ranges combined, deduplicated). Use <code>@@bind-SelectedItems="@@myList"</code> as a shorthand for <code>OnSelectionChanged</code>. Setting this externally also updates the visual selection.</td>
                <td><a href="selection">Selection</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>OnCellClicked</td>
                <td>EventCallback&lt;NxGridCellClickArgs&lt;T&gt;&gt;</td>
                <td>Fires after a clean left-click on a body cell (mousedown and mouseup on the same cell, no drag-select). Does not fire on right-click, header click, keyboard navigation, or <code>SelectRow()</code>. Fires after <code>OnSelectionChanged</code>.</td>
                <td><a href="selection">Selection</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>OnFilterChanged</td>
                <td>EventCallback&lt;NxGridFilterChangedArgs&lt;T&gt;&gt;</td>
                <td>Fires after any column filter changes and the filter pipeline has run. <code>args.Column</code> is null when all filters are cleared at once. <code>args.VisibleItems</code> is the post-filter snapshot.</td>
                <td></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>OnSortChanged</td>
                <td>EventCallback&lt;NxGridSortChangedArgs&lt;T&gt;&gt;</td>
                <td>Fires after the sort column or direction changes. <code>args.Column</code> is null and <code>args.Direction</code> is 0 when sort is cleared. Does not fire when only filter state changes or when state is restored from localStorage.</td>
                <td></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>OnKeyPressed</td>
                <td>EventCallback&lt;NxGridKeyPressedArgs&gt;</td>
                <td>Fires for keyboard events the grid does not handle internally, letting the host page react to custom hotkeys.</td>
                <td><a href="keyboard">Keyboard</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>OnColumnResized</td>
                <td>EventCallback&lt;NxGridColumnResizedArgs&gt;</td>
                <td>Fires when the user drags a resize grip <strong>or double-clicks it to auto-size</strong>, passing <code>ColumnIndex</code> and <code>NewWidth</code>.</td>
                <td></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>OnCellDoubleClicked</td>
                <td>EventCallback&lt;NxGridCellClickArgs&lt;T&gt;&gt;</td>
                <td>Fires on double-click for non-editable columns, passing <code>Row</code> and <code>Column</code>.</td>
                <td><a href="editing">Editing</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>OnContextMenuShowing</td>
                <td>Action&lt;NxGridContextMenuArgs&lt;T&gt;&gt;?</td>
                <td>Called synchronously before the context menu opens; append <code>NxGridContextMenuItem</code> entries to <code>args.Items</code> to add custom items.</td>
                <td><a href="context-menu">Context Menu</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>OnContextMenuItemClicked</td>
                <td>EventCallback&lt;NxGridContextMenuItemArgs&lt;T&gt;&gt;</td>
                <td>Fires when the user selects a custom context menu item.</td>
                <td><a href="context-menu">Context Menu</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>OnRowDrop</td>
                <td>EventCallback&lt;NxGridRowDropArgs&lt;T&gt;&gt;</td>
                <td>Fires after a successful row drag. The host must reorder <code>Data</code> in this handler.</td>
                <td><a href="row-drag-drop">Row Drag &amp; Drop</a></td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

